BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:First Presbyterian Church
DTSTART:20120414T130000Z
DTEND:20120414T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260717T222141Z
UID:69afa1u34mcpiutrfg8b5l3acg@google.com
CREATED:20151027T131257Z
DESCRIPTION:On Saturday\, April 14\, Professor Emeritus of Biology and Geol
 ogy\, David Dilcher\, will lead a walk to view wildflowers.  David is a for
 mer member of our church and is an expert on the origin of flowering plants
 .  He mostly studies fossil plants but also knows a great deal about presen
 t day flowering plants.  We will find a spot for the walk where the flowers
  are especially beautiful.  \n\nWe will walk at a leisurely pace so we can 
 enjoy the flowers.  The walk should thus not be strenuous and probably no m
 ore than a mile or so in length.  We will meet at the church parking lot at
  9:00 and will plan to return by noon.  Please let Bob Dodd (dodd@indiana.e
 du or 339-2976) know if you plan to join us.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20151027T131701Z
LOCATION:Meet at Church Parking Lot
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Presbyterians Outdoors:  Spring Wildflower Walk
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
