DESCRIPTION:Henry James\, Washington Square  (paperback\, various\, c. 160 
 pp.).  Leader: Galina McLaws. Short novel published in 1880 and praised for
  its depiction of the complicated relationship between a stubborn father an
 d his daughter. Cynthia Ozick\, in her introduction to what she calls Henry
  James's "most American fiction\," writes that "every line\, every paragrap
 h\, every chapter is a fleet-footed light brigade\, an engine of irony." Pr
 ecise and understated\, this charming novel endures as a matchless study of
  New York in the mid-19th century.
LAST-MODIFIED:20151027T131701Z
LOCATION:Downstairs Activity Room\, Bell Trace Retirement Community
